card.statement:
For a vector $L=(l_{ij})$ in $\mathbb{C}^{\frac{n(n+1)}{2}}$, by $T(L)$ we will denote the following array with entries $\{l_{ij}:1\leq j\leq i\leq n\}$

\begin{center} \Stone{ {$l_{n1}$}}\Stone{ {$l_{n2}$}} $\dots$ \Stone{ {$l_{n,n-1}$}}\Stone{ {$l_{nn}$}}

[0.2pt] \Stone{ {$l_{n-1,1}$}} $\dots$ \Stone{ {$l_{n-1,n-1}$}}

[0.3cm] $\dots$ $\dots$ $\dots$

[0.3cm] \Stone{ {$l_{21}$}}\Stone{ {$l_{22}$}}

[0.2pt] \Stone{ {$l_{11}$}} \end{center} Such an array will be called a Gelfand--Tsetlin tableau of height $n$. A Gelfand--Tsetlin tableau of height $n$ is called standard if $l_{ki}-l_{k-1,i}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$ and $l_{k-1,i}-l_{k,i+1}\in\mathbb{Z}_{> 0}$ for all $1\leq i\leq k\leq n-1$.
